{"name":"Greek Villa","hex":"#f0ece2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"greek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Greek (“nonsense writing or talk; gibberish”).","Alternative letter-case form of Greek (“anal sex”)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To display a placeholder (instead of text), especially to optimize speed in displaying text that would be too small to read.","To fill a template with nonsense text (particularly the Lorem ipsum), so that form can be focused on instead of content."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greek"},{"term":"villa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A house, often larger and more expensive than average, in the countryside or on the coast, often used as a retreat.","A family house, often semi-detached in Victorian or Edwardian style, in a middle class street."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A country house, with farm buildings around a courtyard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/villa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Villa","blocks":[{"text":"A villa is a type of house that was originally an ancient Roman upper class country house that provided an escape from urban life. Since its origins in the Roman villa, the idea and function of a villa have evolved considerably. After the fall of the Roman Republic, villas became small farming compounds, which were increasingly fortified in Late Antiquity, sometimes transferred to the Church for reuse as a monastery. They gradually re-evolved through the Middle Ages into elegant upper-class country homes. In the early modern period, any comfortable detached house with a garden near a city or town was likely to be described as a villa; most surviving villas have now been engulfed by suburbia. In modern parlance, \"villa\" can refer to various types and sizes of residences, ranging from the suburban semi-detached double villa to, in some countries, especially around the Mediterranean, residences of above average size in the countryside."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Villa_medici_di_belcanto%2C_veduta_00.JPG/330px-Villa_medici_di_belcanto%2C_veduta_00.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa","wikidata":"Q3950"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/TamminiemenhuvilavillaEkudden.JPG/500px-TamminiemenhuvilavillaEkudden.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/TamminiemenhuvilavillaEkudden.JPG/500px-TamminiemenhuvilavillaEkudden.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Villa Tamminiemi, an Art Nouveau styled villa and house museum in Helsinki, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATamminiemenhuvilavillaEkudden.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Villa_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg/500px-Villa_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Villa_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg/1280px-Villa_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Villa_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg/500px-Villa_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Villa of the Mysteries in Pompeii seen from above","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVilla_of_the_Mysteries_in_Pompeii.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Fishbourne_model.JPG/500px-Fishbourne_model.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Fishbo